{"id": 10, "ts": 1780422009.7209601, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m still inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fB. Emily highlighted B\u2019s strong stress handling and conscientiousness, which are critical for long\u2011haul operations. While B can be grumpy and occasionally uncooperative, his proven ability to manage stress and assess weather conditions directly supports the reliability and calm\u2011under\u2011pressure criteria we need.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC, despite being 100\u202f% reliable and creating a positive crew atmosphere, has a documented difficulty communicating ideas. As James noted, we have no concrete evidence of how C performs communication\u2011wise in high\u2011pressure or emergency scenarios, which raises a red flag for decision quality and crew cooperation under stress. Given the safety\u2011critical nature of this role, I view B\u2019s demonstrated stress resilience as a stronger overall fit, provided we address his uncooperative tendencies through onboarding and team\u2011building."}
